        "--prompt-en",
        "A complex photographic scene in a small coastal ferry waiting room, where several visible relationships unfold together as boarding resumes after rain. The reference-guided main subject is a woman seated near the end of a worn wooden bench, turned three quarters toward a suitcase on the adjacent seat. Her visible face and hair are guided by the attached reference: a soft side-parted dark bob, loose fine fringe, rounded dark eyes and delicate brows. Her intent concentration softens into a small, almost private smile at the other passenger's relief; her face feels immediate and quietly appealing in the soft window light. She wears a long pale oatmeal herringbone wool coat open over a cobalt rib-knit top, charcoal twill trousers, and a rust-colored silk neck scarf tied loosely at one side with two distinct tails resting on the coat. A small silver watch closes around her left wrist. At her right waist, the coat's near side panel drops freely away from her flank, leaving an open wedge of air between the blue top's body contour and the wool panel; its open front edges continue down to the upper calves. The long outer garment hangs away from the torso with a visible gap beside its side panel. The coat sleeves crease at her bent elbows. Her brown leather crossbody bag sits just forward of her left hip, its front face and both top corners turned into view, with one diagonal shoulder strap and a brass adjustment buckle. The two distinct strap ends clip separately into brass D-rings fixed to short leather tabs at the two upper corners of this one bag. The same bag's strap supports its body from two visible attachment fittings. The bag stays below and clear of her working forearms. A mustard canvas suitcase rests squarely on the adjacent seat. Dark olive woven webbing encircles its body and ends in a rectangular side-release buckle facing the viewer. Her left thumb and index finger stabilize the buckle housing, and her right hand guides the mating tongue straight into it; the webbing runs through both parts and lies snugly around the case. A second passenger in a sea-green cotton work jacket steadies the suitcase by its top handle, watching her hands with a breath of relief. Both her forearms have clear space above the case, her shoulders remain over her seated hips, and her feet rest on the terrazzo floor. Behind them an attendant begins lifting the simple boarding gate; a white ferry and rain-dark dock are visible through broad windows. Folded wet umbrellas lean in a tray beside the bench, their drops leaving small dark patches. Photograph the connected moment from the seated woman's face height at a nearby three-quarter angle from her right-front side, framing her from the crown to the lower calves with the entire coat hem, the complete buckle, both bag fittings, the second passenger and the gate. Keep her face and the shared fastening action clear, then let the waiting room recede gently. Warm natural skin against the cool gray-blue window light, subdued practical ceiling light, faithful wool, knit, silk, leather and canvas surfaces, natural perspective and fine photographic detail create a humane, observed travel photograph.",
